  "notes": "Talent-show pop that annexed pop-rock, and the harmony is the reason it needs its own model rather than the genre default: the documented signature key is G major with a **G–Am–Em–F** loop — I–ii–vi–IV, \"a non-functional, indie-derived cycle rather than a I–V–vi–IV\" — so that family carries top weight and the canonical pop loop sits under it. 90–132 straight, backbeat on 2&4. The drums are documented as an intervention: \"harder drums\" added at the artist's insistence over a programmed demo, so the accent tier is the highest in this batch and the snare is dry and tight. Three deltas: \"kick 1 and 3 with an 8th pickup\" (second anchor \"4&\"), \"8th hat in verse, crash-and-open-hat 8ths in the chorus\" (an 8th base with a high open-hat probability on both \"&\"s and a crash lane), and \"a one-bar drum-out before the last chorus\", which is `dropOutBeats` at 0.95 over 4 beats. The melody spans a documented two octaves (G3–G5) \"with the chorus apex on the title\" and \"no melisma — straight belted notes\", which is the 55–79 register with a high `chordToneBias`, an arch contour and no end variation. The quiet-verse/loud-chorus alternative-rock dynamic is carried in the arrangement rather than in the notes. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are the drum probabilities and velocity tier — \"harder\" and \"hit hard with a short room\" are directions, and 112–127 is this author's reading.",
